# ReadBoot library architecture

- Only posts in the WordPress category slug `readboot` belong in the ReadBoot library.
- `articleType` is one editorial classification per post; `theories` is one-or-many ReadBoot framework classifications. Neither is a WordPress `tag`.
- Keep WordPress `tags` separate from library filtering and card metadata unless the owner explicitly asks to add them.
- `@repo/wp-utils` owns GraphQL queries, normalization, filter parsing, and filter-option building for library content.
- Shared library UI lives under `packages/ui/src/components/ContentLibrary/` and `packages/ui/src/components/ContentArticle/`, then re-exports through `@repo/ui/sites`.
- `apps/readboot/app/library/` routes stay thin: parse `searchParams`, fetch normalized entries, apply filters, and render shared components.
- Hide or 404 `readboot` posts that are missing `articleType` or `theories` until the content is fully classified.
- Keep the shared components structurally complete but visually minimal so app-level SCSS can own the final presentation.
